9. Agreed next task — Threads educational audit

The project owner agreed to the following approach:

Detailed educational audit of the existing Threads draft, followed by a refined educational blueprint for approval.

The audit will examine:

* Technical accuracy.
* Teaching progression from simple to expert.
* Program, process and thread distinctions.
* Shared resources and individual execution context.
* Thread states and scheduling.
* Kernel-managed and user-level threads.
* Concurrency and parallelism.
* Synchronisation mechanisms.
* Race conditions and deadlocks.
* Thread architecture and mapping models.
* Simulation and diagram requirements.
* Practical examples.
* Knowledge assessment and feedback.
* Alignment between learning objectives and content.
* Content-block organisation within the existing reusable architecture.

The existing material should be retained wherever accurate and useful.

The refined blueprint must be reviewed and approved before implementation.

No Threads files should be changed until the relevant implementation work is explicitly authorised.

